These are hardcover children's books with a continuous narrative and illustrations. Children's picture books fall under heading 4903, "Children's picture books, drawing or coloring books." HTSUS 4903.00.0000 covers them, with statistical suffix 4903.00.0000 at the 10-digit level being 4903.00.0000.

CBP rulings on children's storybooks with illustrations and a story generally classify them in 4903 when the illustrations predominate. The description here says "illustrated pages with text" and a "continuous narrative accompanied by illustrations", which suggests the text may predominate. Ruling language says that a book with a narrative story and illustrations is a children's picture book if the illustrations are the primary value. In this case, the 36-page and 46-page hardcover books are children's picture books, so 4903 applies. Hardbound picture books fall under 4903.00.0000 (the HTS has no separate subdivisions for hardbound), so I'll use 4903.00.0000.

{"hts_code": "4903.00.0000", "reason": "Hardcover illustrated children's storybooks with continuous narrative and illustrations on every page are children's picture books of heading 4903."}
